  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e81bb16ba40385c4bb6dac73ed24daa7, type: 3}
  m_Name: ModelCard
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SimuLean.Unity.SimuLeanModelCard
  displayName: "Workshop \u2014 shared operators, preemption and repairs"
  description: 'Two machining lines share two walking operators: urgent orders take an operator from the normal line (Resume preemption).

    A mechanic repairs the CNC failures, and the operators break down and hand their work over.'
  author: SimuLean
  scenePath: Assets/Scenes/LibraryExamples/Workshop_Resources.unity
  copiedFrom: 
  created: 2026-11-04 12:00:00
  modified: 2026-11-04 12:00:00
  represents: "A machining workshop in one 8 h shift: normal orders (Normal Orders \u2192 Normal Buffer \u2192 CNC A, two spindles \u2192 Inspection \u2192 Shipped) and urgent orders (Urgent Orders \u2192 Urgent Buffer \u2192 CNC B \u2192 Shipped Urgent) share the team Operators (2 walking operators); CNC A asks with priority 1, CNC B with priority 5, both with Resume preemption, so an urgent job takes an operator from CNC A, whose job pauses and resumes where it was.\nThe downtime CNC Failure (MTBF / MTTR on CNC A and CNC B) is repaired by the team Mechanics (1 mechanic, repair priority 10, not preemptable, returns to the maintenance corner); the downtime Operator Breakdown stops each operator (Immediate), who hands the job over to the other (On Stop HandOver). Inspection needs no operator. Left out: setups, material supply, breaks, scrap."
  kpis: "Throughput: normal=Shipped.input, urgent=Shipped Urgent.input (seed 1: 288 and 62 in 8 h).\nPreemption: preemptions=team:Operators.preemptions (47), interruptions of the normal line's jobs CNC A.interruptions, its time paused interruptedA=CNC A.interrupted_time (s; open pauses counted up to the end) and CNC A.interrupted_time_avg (per interruption).\nRepairs: repairWaitA=downtime:CNC Failure@CNC A.repair_wait_avg, repairWaitB=downtime:CNC Failure@CNC B.repair_wait_avg (s, stop \u2192 mechanic there), downtime:CNC Failure@CNC A.repairs, downtime:CNC Failure@CNC A.downtime_total.\nOperator breakdowns: downtime:Operator Breakdown@Operator 1.stops / @Operator 2.\nUtilisation: team:Operators.utilization (0.81), team:Mechanics.utilization (0.24), CNC A.utilization, CNC B.utilization, CNC A.state:WAITING_FOR_RESOURCE."
  parameters: "Urgent priority: CNC B.processBy.priority (5; CNC A 1): a constant priority is a study factor, e.g. CNC B.processBy.priority=1|5 to compare with no priority.\nPreemption modes: CNC A.processBy.preemption / CNC B.processBy.preemption = None|Resume|Restart (Abort never interrupts a station's job); CNC A.processBy.preemptable / CNC B.processBy.preemptable = true|false.\nTeam sizes: team:Operators.members=1..4, team:Mechanics.members=1..2; walking speed team:Operators.speed (1.2 m/s).\nFailures: downtime:CNC Failure.timeToFailure.uniformMin / .uniformMax (uniform 1800..2700 s between failures), downtime:CNC Failure.timeToRepair.triangularMin / .triangularMode / .triangularMax (triangular 180 / 300 / 420 s repair); downtime:Operator Breakdown.timeToFailure.exponentialRate (exponential rate 0.000185 /s = every ~1.5 h), downtime:Operator Breakdown.timeToRepair.uniformMin / .uniformMax (uniform 240..480 s).\nArrivals: Normal Orders.interArrivalDistribution.exponentialRate (0.0111 /s = every 90 s), Urgent Orders.interArrivalDistribution.exponentialRate (0.00238 /s = every 7 min).\nProcess times: CNC A.delayStrategy.triangularMin / Mode / Max (80 / 100 / 125 s), CNC B (150 / 180 / 240 s), Inspection (30 / 45 / 60 s)."
  assumptions: 'One shift of 8 h (horizon 28800 s, time unit s, no warm-up: the run starts empty), fixed seed 1; end condition Stop When No Progress For 1800 s (items waiting and nothing moving).

    Operators and the mechanic walk in straight lines at 1.2 m/s between the work points (no network or grid); the mechanic returns home after each repair, the operators stay where they worked.

    Failures on calendar time (MTBF counted from the end of the repair), Immediate stops blocking the machine''s input; an operator''s breakdown hands the job over to the free operator, else the job waits.

    Buffers of 100 (never full); illustrative times, not calibrated to any plant.'
